        "subject": "LU-21061 lmv: keep deactivated MDTs inactive at mount",
        "message": "LU-21061 lmv: keep deactivated MDTs inactive at mount\n\nA client that mounts while an MDT is deactivated in the configuration\n(lctl conf_param FSNAME-MDTxxxx.mdc.active=0) still uses it:\nlmv_connect_mdc() marks the target active although its MDC import\nstays deactivated.  New directories placed on it fail with -ESHUTDOWN,\nand lmv_statfs() and lfs df ask it for statistics.\n\nTake ltd_active from the deactivated flag of the MDC import in\nlmv_connect_mdc(), as LOV leaves an administratively disabled OSC\ninactive, and set OBDF_INACTIVE to match; reactivation still goes\nthrough lmv_notify().  Count only active targets when\nlmv_check_connect() fails, and give inactive MDTs the EA sizes too, so\nthey have them once activated.  Skip inactive MDTs in lmv_statfs(),\nwhich now starts the sum from the first MDT that answers rather than\nthe first one tried, and returns -ENODATA when none does.  This also\nfixes a sum whose first MDT failed, which was added to a result that\nwas never set.  Also stop OST0001 at the end of conf-sanity\ntest_50i, which stopped OST0000 twice and left OST0001 mounted for\nthe next test.\n\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I1e1abdd758fdefbd51ba9e27bd957d016f0cdbf8\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
